From be967b1ecea6095c723102e21467128a61219fd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:51:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows: Wind Waker HD's cascade splits from the game's
 camera each frame

aurora_set_sun_cascade_splits(middle, far): HD sets its shadow cascades' splits each frame from its camera
(its distance to what it looks at and its field of view) and fits its first two cascades to the slices they
make. The HD quality's splits (now in the pass's uniform, in place of constants) and its first two cascades'
sizes follow them; 0 keeps the fixed ones (420 and 1395, HD's at Outset's bridge; DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_HD_SPLITS
sets them for tests). With fixed ones, BlueWake's camera zoomed out (the mouse wheel's 2x) left Star Island in
the far cascade's 18-unit texels and its grass's shadows crawled as the sun turned; the shadow's change from
frame to frame over the grass fell from 3.6 to 2.4 (worst frame 4.7% to 2.8% of pixels).

Also a test of HD's pre-pass taking the farthest of the four depth texels under each of its pixels (agl's
shadow_pre_pass.sh, USE_FETCH_4; DOL_AURORA_SUN_SHADOW_PREPASS_FAR=1). It barely changed the palms' crowns
(45% to 43% of leaf pixels shaded below 0.9, against HD's 13%); off by default.
